// `@storage` with a BARE enumeration value.
//
// `etch-grammar.md` §1.5 admits a bare `IDENT` for `annotation_arg`, so this
// parses; it is refused on schema grounds, not grammatical ones. An argument
// whose declared type is an enumeration domain is written as a tag path —
// `@storage(.sparse)` — which is what every sibling annotation of that shape
// already does (`@phase`, `@tag`, `@pause_group`, dotted in every occurrence
// of the corpus).
//
// The decisive reason is ambiguity, not uniformity: a bare enumeration value
// is syntactically indistinguishable from an identifier reference, so `sparse`
// can collide with a type or a variable of that name and `.sparse` cannot.
//
// The bare form lived in the corpus for one reason: `@storage` was a no-op, so
// its spelling had never met an execution path. Reversed at the G1 verdict.
//
// Expected: E0503 AnnotationArgMismatch (§13.3 step 3 — spelling), and NOT
// E0504: `sparse` is a value the domain has, so "must be a constant" would be
// false about the value and silent about what to write instead.

@storage(sparse)
component Chilled {
    stacks: int = 1
}
